/* SPECULATIVE SCORE-DRAFT STARTER */

const bpm = 161;

// Main Kick: Use a MembraneSynth with a sharp attack (0.001) and heavy drive (~0.8) to get the punch and grit.
// Pattern: ['C1', null, null, null, 'C1', null, null, null, ...]

// Snare: A NoiseSynth with 'white' noise, a very fast envelope (attack: 0.001, decay: 0.15), and a bandpass filter around 3kHz with some Q.
// Pattern: [null, null, null, null, 'x', null, null, null, ...]

// Hats: MetalSynth is key. For the main 16ths, use a high frequency, low harmonicity (e.g., 1.1), and a very short decay (~0.08). 
// Pattern: ['x', 'x', 'x', 'x', ...]

// Textures: FMSynth for the atmospheric scrapes. Use a long ADSR (release ~4s), high modulationIndex (~15) and harmonicity (~3.2) for a complex, inharmonic tone. Drench in reverb (reverbSend > 0.8).

// Effects: Route most percussion tracks through a master distortion or bitcrusher effect with a moderate wet/dry mix to glue them together and add overall grit. A master reverb can provide the sense of space.
